      "evidence": "The title calls this “A uniformly gapped occupied-projector response map,” but the Definition sets Φ(X) whenever the gap at that individual X is strict; its separate uniform-gap clause requires a common g>0 only for every X in a set K. The in-scope example H(t)=diag(-t,t) has Φ defined for all t∈(0,1], although the gaps 2t have infimum 0 on that set. Thus the title overstates the domain condition defined.",
